==Swedish==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|sv}} {{term|fé|lang=non}} from {{proto|Germanic|fehu|lang=sv}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|peḱu-|livestock, domestic animals|lang=sv}}. Cognate with Latin {{term|pecu||heard, flock|lang=la}}, {{term|pecus||sheep, animal|lang=la}}, {{term|pecunia||money|lang=la}}; Gothic {{term|faihu||wealth|lang=got}}, Old English {{term|feoh||livestock, money|lang=ang}} (English {{term|fee|lang=en}}) Old Saxon {{term|fehu}}, Old High German {{term|fihu}} (Dutch {{term|vee||cattle}}, German {{term|Vieh||cattle|lang=de}}), Danish {{term|fæ|lang=da}} and Swedish {{term|fä||cattle|lang=sv}}.

